              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+adjunctions"} strong monoidal adjunctions
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            for which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
            so that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            is, canonically, a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            to that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+categories"} monoidal model categories
            %strong lax monoidal Quillen adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi L
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (L \dashv R) : C \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}}
                  D
          %p is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
                between the underlying
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            %li
              %p
                equipped with the structure of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                with respect to the underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            %li
              %p
                such that the induced structure of an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oplax+monoidal+functor"} oplax monoidal functor
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                satisfies:
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    for all cofibrant objects
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in D
                    the oplax monoidal transformation
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mo ∇
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                          %mo :
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          \\tilde\nabla_{x,y} : L(x \otimes y) \to L(x) \otimes L(y)
                  %p
                    is a weak equivalence in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %li
                  %p
                    for some (hence any) cofibrant
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi q
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi I
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mi D
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ≃
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q : \hat I_D \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} I_D
                    of the monoidal unit object in
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi I
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi L
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi q
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mover
                              %mi e
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          L(\hat I_D) \stackrel{L(q)}{\to} L(I_D) \stackrel{\tilde e}{\to} I_C
                  %p
                    with the oplax monoidal counit is a weak equivalence in
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi C
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            This is called a
            %strong strong monoidal Quillen adjunction
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is vacuous, and the second becomes vacuous if the unit object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is cofibrant.
          %p
            If a monoidal Quillen adjunction is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            it is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong monoidal Quillen equivalence
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#Recognition Recognition of monoidal Quillen adjunctions
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R) : C \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}} D
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+categories"} monoidal model categories
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be equipped with the strcuture of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
            %p
              Then the following two conditions are sufficient for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
              to be a lax monoidal Quillen adjunction:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  for some (hence any) cofibrant
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi I
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mi D
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q : \hat I_D \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} I_D
                  of the unit object in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi I
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mover
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        L(\hat I_D) \stackrel{L(q)}{\to} L(I_D) \stackrel{\tilde i}{\to} I_C
                %p
                  is a weak equivalence, (wher
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde i
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
                  of
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi D
                          %mo →
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : I_D \to R(I_C)
              %li
                %p
                  the unit object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_D
                  %em detects weak equivalences
                  in that for every weak equivalence
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
                  between fibrant objects the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi D
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi op
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Q
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^{\Delta^{op}}(Q I_D, f)
                  of
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  is an equivalence of Kan complexes, for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Q
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q I_D
                  a cofibrant resolution in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi D
                            %mi Reedy
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi Δ
                                %mi op
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^{\Delta^{op}}_{Reedy}
          %p
            This is proposition 3.16 in (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley"}> SchwedeShipley
            ).
          %h3#LiftToAdjunctionOnMonoids Lift to an adjunction on monoids
          %p
            We discuss how a monoidal Quillen adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi L
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R) : C \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}} D
            induces, under mild conditions, an adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi mon
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi L
                  %mi Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L^{mon} \dashv R) : Mon(C) \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}} Mon(D)
            on the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+monoids"} categories of monoids
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R : C \to D
            induces (as described there) a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R : Mon(C) \to Mon(D)
            on monoids (which by slight abuse of notation we denote by the same symbol). Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi R
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_{X,Y} : R X \otimes R Y \to R(X \otimes Y)
            for the lax monoidal structure on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oplax+monoidal+functor"} oplax monoidal functor
            (as described there) on the left adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L : D \to C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo :
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi L
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde\nabla : L(X \otimes Y) \to L X \otimes L Y
            for this oplax structure.
          %p
            While
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            will not extend to a functor on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+monoids"} category of monoids
            unless
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
            there is nevertheless an adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi mon
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{mon}
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R : Mon(C) \to Mon(D)
          %p
            As described at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+monoids"} category of monoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has countable
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+functor"} free functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi F
                  %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (F \dashv U) : Mon(C) \stackrel{\overset{F}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{U}{\to}}
                  C
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+algebra"} tensor algebra
            over the object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, \otimes)
          #AdjunctionOnMonoids.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R) : C \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}} D
              be a pair of adjoint functors between monoidal categories where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a lax monoidal functor and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              has all small colimits.
            %p
              Then the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R : Mon(C) \to Mon(D)
              has a left adjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mo :
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L^{mon} : Mon(D) \to Mon(C)
            %p
              given by forming the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ↦
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi C
                    %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi D
                    %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi C
                    %mi L
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L^{mon} : B
                    \\mapsto
                    \\lim_{\to}
                    (F_C L F_D B \stackrel{\to}{\to} F_C L B)
            %p
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(C)
              of the following two morphisms
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the first one is the image under
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi C
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_C \circ L
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} adjunction counit
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi D
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi D
                          %mi B
                          %mo →
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_D U_D B  \to B
              %li
                %p
                  the second is the unique
                  = succeed "-monoid" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  = succeed "-morphism" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi D
                        %mi B
                        %mo ≃
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi B
                          %mrow
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                            %mover
                              %mo ∇
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mi B
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi n
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi C
                        %mi L
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        L F_D B
                        \\simeq
                        \\coprod_{n \in \mathbb{N}} L( B^{\otimes n})
                        \\stackrel{\coprod \tilde \nabla}{\to}
                        \\coprod_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
                        (L B)^{\otimes n}
                        \\simeq
                        F_C L B
                %p
                  which is componentwise given by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oplax+monoidal+functor"} oplax monoidal structure
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                  induced by the lax monoidal structure on
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            This is considered on p. 305 of (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley"}> SchwedeShipley
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              To see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L^{mon} \dashv R)
              first notice that a morphism of monoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L^{mon} X \to Y
            %p
              is by the definition of coequalizer a morphism of monoids
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi C
                    %mi L
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : F_C L X \to Y
              satisfying a condition. By the free property of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi C
                    %mi L
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_C L X
              this in turn is a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi L
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1 : L X \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              which by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
              is a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f_1 : X \to R Y
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is precisely the condition that makes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f_1
              a morphism of monoids in that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ⊗
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi R
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \otimes X &amp;\stackrel{\tilde f_1 \otimes \tilde f_1}{\to}&amp; R  Y \otimes R  Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; R ( Y \otimes  Y)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{\tilde f_1}{\to}&amp; R  Y
                    }
            %p
              commutes. We insert the definition of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f_1
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+natural+transformation"} lax naturality
              square of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              to get
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi L
                            %mi X
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi R
                            %mi L
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi R
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi R
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi R
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mi X
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi L
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi R
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \otimes X
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    R L X \otimes R L X
                    \&amp;\stackrel{R f_1 \otimes R f_1}{\to}&amp; R  Y \otimes R  Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;=&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; R(L X \otimes L Y) &amp;\stackrel{R f_1}{\to}&amp; R ( Y \otimes  Y)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp; &amp;\stackrel{\tilde f_1}{\to}&amp;&amp; R  Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of the left/bottom composite is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L(X\otimes X) \to L X \stackrel{f_1}{\to} Y
            %p while the adjunct of the top/right composite is that of the diagonal, which is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mo ∇
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi L
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi L
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⊗
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L(X \otimes X) \stackrel{\tilde \nabla}{\to} L X \otimes L X
                    \\stackrel{f_1 \otimes f_1}{\to} Y \otimes Y \to Y
                    \\,.
            %p
              This in turn is by the definition of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in terms of its components equal to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mo ∇
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi L
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi L
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L(X \otimes X) \stackrel{\tilde \nabla}{\to} L X \otimes L X
                    \\stackrel{f_2}{\to}Y
                    \\,.
            %p The coequalizer property says indeed precisely that these two adjuncts are equal.
          #LemmaOnNaturalIso.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi D
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi C
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi L
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L^{mon} \circ F_D
                    \\simeq
                    F_C \circ L
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is considered on p. 305 of (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley"}> SchwedeShipley
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              On a monoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mi F
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mi L
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L^{mon} F K \to F L K
            %p is defined as a coequalizing morphism of monoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi L
                    %mi F
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mi L
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F L F K \to F L K
                    \\,.
            %p
              This in turn is given by a morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi F
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mi L
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L F K \to F L K
                    \\,.
            %p
              Take this to be given componentwise by the oplax counit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde e
            %p This does coequalize then: for one route is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mo ∇
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L( (K) \otimes (K)  ) \to L(K \otimes K) \stackrel{\tilde \nabla}{\to} L(K) \otimes L(K)
            %p and the other
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mo ∇
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi L
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi L
                    %mi K
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi Id
                    %mi L
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi L
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K( (K) \otimes (K) ) \stackrel{\tilde \nabla}{\to} L K \otimes L K
                    \\stackrel{Id}{\to}
                    L K \otimes L K
                    \\,.
          %h3#LiftToQuillenAdjunctionOnMonoids Lift to a Quillen equivalence on monoids
          %p
            We now describe how the adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi mon
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L^{mon} \dashv R)
            established above becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            for the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred model structure
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} forgetful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+functor"} free functor
            adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi C
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi F
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (F_C \dashv U_C) : Mon(C) \stackrel{\overset{F}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{U}{\to}}
                  C
          %p
            and how it becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
            is a monoidal Quillen eqivalence.
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+monoids"} model structure on monoids
          .un_assumptio
            %h6#assumption Assumption
            %p
              We assume for this section that the monoidal model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
              %li
                %p
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
              %li
                %p
                  satisfies the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+axiom+in+a+monoidal+model+category"} monoid axiom in a monoidal model category
          %p
            Then by (
            %a{:href => "SchwedeShipleyAlgebras"}> SchwedeShipleyAlgebras
            ) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+monoids+in+a+monoidal+model+category"} model structure on monoids in a monoidal model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(C)
            exists.
          %p
            Notice also that by cofibrant generation every cofibrant object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(C)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
            of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \dashv U)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+object"} cell object
          %p =–
          #LiftedQuillenAdjunction.un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R) : C \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}} D
              be a lax monoidal Quillen adjunction between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+categories"} monoidal model categories
              with cofibrant unit obects.
            %p Then also the adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi L
                            %mi mon
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L^{mon} \dashv R)
                    \:
                    Mon(C) \stackrel{\overset{L^{mon}}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}} Mon(D)
                    \\,,
            %p
              from
              %a{:href => "#AdjunctionOnMonoids"} above
              is a Quillen adjunction between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+monoids"} model structures on monoids
            %p
              If the forgetful functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_D
              %a{:href => "#CreatedModelStructure"} create
              model structures on monoids, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L^{mon} \dashv R)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
              is.
          %p
            This is theorem 3.12 in (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley"}> SchwedeShipley
            ). Its proof uses the following technical lemmas.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi L
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R) : C \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}} D
            be a monoidal Quillen adjunction between monoidal model categories with cofibrant unit objects.
          %p Suppose the adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi mon
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi L
                  %mi Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (L^{mon} \dashv R)
                  \:
                  Mon(C) \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}} Mon(D)
          %p described above exists (just as an adjunction, not yet assumed to be a Quillen adjunction).
          #VeryFirstTechnicalLemma.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p The morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L^{mon} I_D \to I_C
            %p
              induced by the oplax counit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo :
                    %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde e : L I_D \to I_C
              of the oplax monoidal functor is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              of monoids.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              We have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_D
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_C
              are the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(D)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mon
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{mon}
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %em some
              isomorphism as claimed. It is hence sufficient to show that the oplax counit induces a morphism of monoids at all, by the universal property of the initial object it will be an isomorphism.
            %p It is clear that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\coprod_n \mu^n {\tilde e}^{\otimes n} : F L I_D \to I_C
            %p is a morphism of monoids, because
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mi I
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi k
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mi I
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mi k
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi I
                                  %mi k
                                %msup
                                  %mover
                                    %mi e
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %mi k
                                %mo ⊗
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi I
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo −
                                    %mi k
                                %msup
                                  %mover
                                    %mi e
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo −
                                    %mi k
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi I
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi I
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mi I
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi I
                                  %mi n
                                %msup
                                  %mover
                                    %mi e
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                  %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (L I)^{\otimes k} \otimes (L I)^{\otimes (n-k)}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mu_I^k {\tilde e}^{\otimes k} \otimes \mu_I^{n-k}{\tilde e}^{\otimes (n-k)}}{\to}&amp;
                    I \otimes I
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    (L I)^{\otimes n}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mu^n_I {\tilde e}^{n}}{\to}&amp; I
                    }
            %p
              commutes. So we have to show that this morphism coequalizes the two morphisms in the definition of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mi mon
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{mon} I_D
              %a{:href => "#AdjunctionOnMonoids"} above proof
              this is equivalent to showing that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi C
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi e
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi e
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi C
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi R
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi C
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi C
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi e
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    I_C \otimes I_C &amp;\stackrel{e \otimes e}{\to}&amp;
                    R I_C \otimes R I_C
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; R (I_C \otimes I_C)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    I_C &amp;\stackrel{e}{\to}&amp; R I_C
                    }
            %p
              commutes. This follows from the unitality of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          #OneTechnicalLemma.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_3 Lemma
            %p
              For every monoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in Mon(D)
              which is an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \dashv U)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+object"} cell object
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %mi L
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi_B :  L B \to L^{mon} B
            %p
              to the morphism underlying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to R L^{mon} B
              is a weak equivalence.
          %p
            This is proposition 5.1 in (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley"}> SchwedeShipley
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              We first show this for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = I_D
              the tensor unit in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(D)
              is the
              = succeed "s:" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  We claim hat the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} adjunction unit
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                        %msup
                          %mi L
                          %mi mon
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi D
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ≃
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_C \to R L^{mon} I_D \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} R(I_C)
                  is the lax monoidal unit
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %p
                  To see this, use that by the
                  %a{:href => "#VeryFirstTechnicalLemma"} previous lemma
                  the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi L
                          %mo ⊣
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                        %msup
                          %mi L
                          %mi mon
                        %mi I
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \to R L^{mon} I \to R I
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mi I
                          %mo →
                          %msup
                            %mi L
                            %mi mon
                          %mi I
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                                %mi n
                              %msup
                                %mi μ
                                %mi n
                              %msup
                                %mover
                                  %mi e
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi n
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L I \to L^{mon} I \stackrel{\coprod_n \mu^n {\tilde e}^{\otimes n}}{\to} I
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L I
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mover
                            %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mo :
                          %mi L
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi D
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde e : L I_D \to I_C
                %p
                  Therefore by the axioms on monoidal Quillen adjunctions the
                  = succeed "-adjunct" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi L
                          %mo ⊣
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_I
                  is a weak equivalence.
            %p
              We now proceed from this by induction over the cells of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+object"} cell object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %p
              So assume now that we have already shown that on some cell object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_B
              is a weak equivalence. We want to deduce then that that after forming a new monoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              by cell attachment, i.e. by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mi K
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mi K
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    F K &amp;\to&amp; F K'
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\to&amp; P
                    }
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \to K'
              a cofibration in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mi L
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_P : L P \to L^{mon} P
              is a weak equivalence.
            %p
              Notice that since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{mon}
              is left adjoint also
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi L
                              %mi mon
                            %mi F
                            %mi K
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi L
                              %mi mon
                            %mi F
                            %mi K
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi L
                              %mi mon
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi L
                              %mi mon
                            %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    L^{mon} F K &amp;\to&amp; L^{mon} F K'
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    L^{mon} B &amp;\to&amp; L^{mon} P
                    }
            %p
              is a pushout in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mon
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(C)
              %a{:href => "#LemmaOnNaturalIso"} the above lemma
              so is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mi L
                            %mi K
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mi L
                            %mi K
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi L
                              %mi mon
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi L
                              %mi mon
                            %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    F L K &amp;\to&amp; F L K'
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    L^{mon} B &amp;\to&amp; L^{mon} P
                    }
                    \\,.
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  We claim that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  is cofibrant and that we can without restriction assume
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K'
                  to be cofibrant in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                %p
                  The first statement follows from an inductive application of the construction of pushouts as discussed at
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+monoids"} category of monoids
                  in the section
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/category+of+monoids#FreeMonoids"} free monoids
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is left adjoint and preserves pushouts in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                  is also the pushout of the diagram
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi F
                                  %mi B
                                %mtd
                                  %mo →
                                %mtd
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi B
                                  %munder
                                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                                    %mi K
                                  %mi K
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi B
                                %mtd
                                  %mo →
                                %mtd
                                  %mi P
                          %mo )
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mi F
                                  %mi K
                                %mtd
                                  %mo →
                                %mtd
                                  %mi F
                                  %mi K
                                  %mo ′
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi F
                                  %mi B
                                %mtd
                                  %mo →
                                %mtd
                                  %mi F
                                  %mi B
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi B
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mo →
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mi P
                          %mo )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\left(
                        \\array{
                        F B &amp;\to&amp; F( B \coprod_K K' )
                        \\\
                        \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                        \\\
                        B &amp;\to&amp; P
                        }
                        \\right)
                        \=
                        \\left(
                        \\array{
                        \&amp;&amp; F K &amp;\to&amp; F K'
                        \\\
                        \&amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                        \\\
                        F B &amp;\to&amp; F B
                        \\\
                        \\downarrow &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                        \\\
                        B &amp;&amp; \to &amp;&amp; P
                        }
                        \\right)
                        \\,.
                %p
                  Since cofibrations are preserved by the Quillen left adjoint
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  and under pushout, it follows that also
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mi K
                        %mi K
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \coprod_K K'
                  is cofibrant if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo →
                        %mi K
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \to K'
                  is a cofibration. So
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mi K
                        %mi K
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to B \coprod_K K'
                  can be used in place of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mo →
                          %mi K
                          %mo ′
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \to K'
            %p
              Notice that this means that our pushout square is in fact a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
              square (as discussed there). In particular a weak equivalence of these pushout diagrams will induce a weak equivalence of the pushouts, so that is what we will establish.
            %p
              We now proceed as in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+monoids"} category of monoids
              in the section
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/category+of+monoids#FreeMonoids"} free monoids
              for getting the following statement about the object underlying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %p
              This
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              of a sequence of cofibrations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    P \simeq \lim_{\to} ( B := P_0 \hookrightarrow P_1 \hookrightarrow P_2 \hookrightarrow \cdots )
            %p
              such that each morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} hookrightarow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_{n-1} \hookrightarow P_n
              is a pushout in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              of a particular cofibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo ,
                    %mi K
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi K
                    %mo ′
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi n
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_n(K,K', B) \hookrightarrow (B \otimes K')^{\otimes n} \otimes B
            %p
              By the coresponding disccussion of these pushouts under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{mon}
              it follows that also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{mon} P
              is the colimit of a sequence of cofibrations betwen objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_n
              that are pushouts of these particular cofibrations.
            %p
              And the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_P
              respects all that and sends
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi P
                          %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi_{P_n} : L P_n \to L^{mon} R_n
            %p
              at each stage of the cell attachments. So it is sufficient to show that the three components of these maps on the pushout squares are weak equivalences. Since we showed above that our pushout squares are actually
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
              squares, this will imply that also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_P
              is a weak equivalence.
            %p
              This again works by proceeding as in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+monoids"} category of monoids
              in the section
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/category+of+monoids#FreeMonoids"} free monoids
          #AnotherTechnicalLemma.un_lemma
            %h6#lemma_4 Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_C
              %a{:href => "#CreatedModelStructure"} creates
              the model structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(C)
              and the unit in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is cofibrant, then a cofibrant
              = succeed "-monoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              This is once more a consequence of the lemma on pushouts at at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+monoids"} category of monoids
              in the section
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/category+of+monoids#FreeMonoids"} free monoids
          %p
            We have now collected all prerequisites and turn to the proof of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#LiftedQuillenAdjunction"} theorem about lifted Quillen adjunctions
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_the_theorem Proof of the theorem
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L^{mon} \dashv R)
              is a Quillen adjunction is clear, as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+monoids"} model structure on monoids
              has fibrations and acyclic fibrations those in the underlying category, and these are preserved by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %p
              So the essential statement is that it is a Quillen equivalence of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
              is.
            %p
              First notice that since by assumption the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+monoids"} model structure on monoids
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(D)
              is
              %a{:href => "#CreatedModelStructure"} created
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_D
              it follows by definition that the cofibrant
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+object"} cell object
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mon
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(D)
              %a{:href => "#OneTechnicalLemma"} above lemma
              asserts that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %mi L
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi_B : L B \to L^{mon} B
            %p is a weak equivalence.
            %p
              To prove the theorem, we have to show for every cofibrant
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in Mon(D)
              and fibrant
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \in Mon(C)
              that a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to R Y
              is a weak equivalence in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(D)
              (hence its underlying morphism in
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{mon} B \to Y
              is a weak equivalence in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(C)
              (hence its underlying morphism in
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              By definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (B \to R Y) = ( B \to R L^{mon} B  \to R Y)
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the
              %a{:href => "#AnotherTechnicalLemma"} second lemma above
              we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is cofibrant also in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
              is a Quillen equivalence between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              = succeed "-adjunct" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L B \stackrel{\chi_B}{\to} L^{mon} B \to Y
            %p
              is a weak equivalence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_B
              is a weak equivalence, this is the case precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi mon
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{mon}B \to Y
              is a weak equivalence.
          %h2#examples Examples
          #Stabilization.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
                in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
              adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mn ∞
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spaces
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    \\Sigma^\infty(-)_+
                    \\dashv
                    \\Omega^\infty
                    \\right)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Ho(Spectra)
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{\Omega^\infty}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\Sigma^\infty(-)}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    Ho(Spaces)
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spaces
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spaces)
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spectra)
              is a monoidal adjunction, since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty(-)_+
              (forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
              of a space after freely
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} adjoining a basepoint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal
              with respect to forming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+spaces"} product topological spaces
              and forming
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+adjunction"} monoidal adjunction
            %p
              In fact this is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
              of what is even a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Quillen+adjunction"} monoidal Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi orth
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi orth
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi OrthSpec
                      %mi stable
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi orth
                            %mn ∞
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi orth
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Sigma^\infty_{orth}(-)_+ \dashv \Omega^\infty_{orth})
                    \\;\colon\;
                    OrthSpec_{stable}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{\Omega_{orth}^\infty}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\Sigma_{orth}^\infty(-)_+}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {}
                    Top_{Quillen}
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
              and the stable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+orthogonal+spectra"} model structure on orthogonal spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#StableMonoidalQuillenSuspensionSpectrumFunctor"}> this cor.
              ) which implies (strong) modality of the derived functors on homotopy categories (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#StrongMonoidalDerivedFunctorFromStrongMonoidalQuillenAdjunction"}> this prop.
              ).
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Examples arise in the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
            %li
              %p
                The quivalence between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
                is exhibited by monoidal Quillen equivalences. See
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectrum"} module spectrum
                for details.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+Quillen+adjunction"} simplicial Quillen adjunction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            %li
              %p
                %strong monoidal Quillen adjunction
          %h2#references References
          %p The notion of strong monoidal Quillen adjunction is def. 4.2.16 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Hovey"}> Mark Hovey
              ,
              %em Model Categories
              Mathematical Surveys and Monographs, Volume 63, AMS (1999) (
              %a{:href => "https://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/hovey-model-cats.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://books.google.co.uk/books?id=Kfs4uuiTXN0C&printsec=frontcover"} Google books
          %p The lax monoidal version is considered as definition 3.6 of
          %ul
            %li#SchwedeShipley
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
              %em Equivalences of monoidal model categories
              , Algebr. Geom. Topol. 3 (2003), 287–334 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0209342"}> arXiv:math.AT/0209342
              )
          %p The statements involving pushouts along free monoid morphisms are discussed in lemma 6.2 of
          %ul#SchwedeShipleyAlgebras
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
              %em Algebras and modules in monoidal model categories
              Proc. London Math. Soc. (2000) 80(2): 491-511 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uic.edu/~bshipley/monoidal.pdf"}> pdf
              )
